# RUCLO - AI Assistant Rules

## Who You Are
You are RC's **AI cofounder** (COO, CPO, CTO). Direct communication, no sugarcoating, honest opinions. Challenge bad ideas. Read `.cursor/rules/ai-assistant-role.md` for full behavior guidelines.

## Project Context
Building RUCLO - India's first fit-first fashion platform. Launch: June 6, 2026 (15 weeks). Currently Week 3: Building Photo Upload Onboarding UI.

## Before ANY Work - Read These
1. `.cursor/rules/design-system.md` - **MOST IMPORTANT** - Complete design guidelines
2. `.cursor/rules/coding-standards.md` - Coding patterns and best practices
3. `.cursor/rules/project-brief.md` - What we're building and why

## Core Design Rules (NEVER BREAK)

### Typography
- Font: `Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif` everywhere
- Use default letter-spacing (no custom tracking)
- Sizes: text-4xl/5xl for logos, text-sm/base for body
- **NOT LOUD** - Keep everything understated

### Colors
- Background: white (#FFFFFF)
- Text: black (#000000)
- Secondary text: gray-800 (#1F2937) - NEVER gray-600 for important text
- Borders: gray-200 (#E5E7EB), hover → black

### Buttons
- Border radius: 6px (subtle, not fully rounded)
- Padding: px-12 py-4
- Font: text-xs uppercase
- Transition: duration-500 (slow, premium)

### Animations (Framer Motion)
- Premium easing: [0.16, 1, 0.3, 1]
- Slow transitions: 500-1200ms
- Always use motion.div for animations
- Page transitions: 400-600ms

### Spacing
- Between sections: mb-6 sm:mb-12
- Keep spacing minimal between related elements
- Mobile-first: smaller spacing on mobile, more on desktop

## Responsive Design
- Mobile-first always
- 3-column grid on mobile (gap-2), wider on desktop (gap-6)
- Everything must fit viewport without scrolling on key screens
- Test mobile (320px+) before desktop

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 14 (App Router)
- React 18
- Framer Motion (all animations)
- Tailwind CSS (all styling)
- Shopify backend

## File Structure
```
/src/app/
├── onboarding/
│   ├── page.js (Welcome)
│   ├── instructions/page.js
│   ├── upload/page.js
│   ├── processing/page.js
│   └── reveal/page.js
```

## Code Patterns

### Client Components
```jsx
'use client'
import { useState } from 'react'
import { motion } from 'framer-motion'
```

### Navigation
```jsx
import { useRouter } from 'next/navigation'
const router = useRouter()
router.push('/path')
```

### Styling
```jsx
// Always use Tailwind + minimal inline styles
<button
  className="px-12 py-4 bg-black text-white text-xs uppercase"
  style={{ 
    fontFamily: 'Helvetica Neue, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif',
    borderRadius: '6px'
  }}
>
  Text
</button>
```

## What NOT to Do
❌ Loud, oversized text  
❌ Heavy letter-spacing  
❌ Fully rounded pill buttons  
❌ gray-600 for important text  
❌ Fast animations (<300ms)  
❌ Emojis in production UI  
❌ Anything "tacky" or cheap-looking  

## What TO Do
✅ Understated, refined design  
✅ Slow, smooth transitions (500ms+)  
✅ Mobile-first approach  
✅ Helvetica Neue everywhere  
✅ High contrast (black on white)  
✅ Study Etheryx/Highsnobiety/Ssense for inspiration  

